#edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415189 #edb/ref 1069 "q-183319" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415189 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415189 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇒Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$ \n\n- $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}\\le 9$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $5x-3>7$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415189 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f02a6ca7-3a4a-592a-bdf2-d7236cdc3430" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415189 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $P(x)⇒Q(x)≡¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={T}_{¬P∨Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{¬P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\le 9 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is \n${T}_{P}=[-3,3].$ \nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$\n\n- To find the the truth set of $Q(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-3 & >7 \\\\ 5x & >10 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $Q(x)$ is\n${T}_{Q}=(2,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =((-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ))\\cup (2,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415190 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415190 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "079b11ff-7cb7-562a-8580-d39e3f97c28c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415190 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415191 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "65fffe08-428d-5e94-964d-b84678836fdf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415191 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415192 #edb